# Files that stay in the repository but must not travel in the delivery.
# `git archive` builds the shipped source snapshot, so anything tracked ends up
# in front of the reader unless it is marked here. A session log reached the
# submission this way once, and the decision log would have followed it.
docs/notes.md export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
# The whole archive of retired working documents, by directory rather than by file.
# it, which silently defeated the `docs/phase*-plan.md` rule below, because that pattern
# matches one level only. `tests/test_delivery_privacy.py` caught it.
# The archive of retired engines, spent probes and past-round logs. Kept in git so
# posterity survives a fresh clone, kept out of the delivery so the reviewer gets
# the working pipeline rather than its history.
legacy/ export-ignore
legacy/** export-ignore
# The round's internal plan and the agent handoff. They are working documents about
# how to approach the reviewer's feedback, not deliverables, and the handoff states
# the working agreement in terms that are nobody's business but ours. `git archive`
# would otherwise put both in front of him: that is exactly how an email draft's
# private section reached the 2 August archive.
docs/phase5-plan.md export-ignore
# Every later round's plan, by pattern rather than one line per round. `phase6-plan.md`
# shipped on 2026-08-18 while the identical phase-5 file was withheld, because the rule
# lived as one filename instead of as a shape.
docs/phase*-plan.md export-ignore
# **Anything addressed to a person.** `submissions/phase-5/email-draft.md` opens "Send to:
# michael.xiaowei.ding@gmail.com" and "Dear Professor Ding", and travelled to Ding inside
# every archive; `docs/report-sendable.md` is the same document's prose and additionally
# carried superseded round-5 figures beside a round-6 report. The house rule is that
# nothing addressed to a person is tracked at all, and `private/` is where drafts belong;
# these two are already in history, so this is the containment. `tests/test_delivery_privacy.py`
# fails if the shape reappears.
submissions/*/email-draft.md export-ignore
docs/report-sendable.md export-ignore
# The agent's short review surface for open and closed decisions. Working
# document about how to approach the round, same class as notes.md.
docs/key-decisions.md export-ignore
# The handoff documents, by pattern rather than one line each. Same class as the plans
# and the decision log: working documents about how to approach the round, and
# corrections owed. Neither is a deliverable and neither is his business.
handoff-*.md export-ignore
